{
  "title": "Cellar Assistant — Actor Observability",
  "uid": "cellar-actor-observability",
  "id": null,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "tags": ["cellar-assistant", "actors", "outbox", "dapr"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "time": { "from": "now-6h", "to": "now" },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "description": "E3b: outbox dead-letter health (the alert rules in ../../alerting/outbox-and-actor-alerts.yaml key on the same queries as the panels below), unexpected actor errors, recent Dapr actor-call traces, and the Dapr runtime's own Prometheus metrics (sidecars, placement, scheduler). The services/api row at the bottom reads the api's own events (graphql.unexpected_error, auth.token_rejected, graphql.limit_refused, actor.invocation_failed, telemetry.suppressed).",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Outbox health",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "removeFriendOtherSide dead-letters (24h)",
      "description": "target-stack.md §7: a dead-lettered removeFriendOtherSide fails open — the surviving friends row keeps the removed person FRIENDS-visible. This must read 0. Anything else is the specific incident the alert rule of the same name fires on.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=\"outbox.dead_letter\" | outbox_method=\"removeFriendOtherSide\" [24h])) OR vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 1 }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": { "match": "null+nan", "result": { "text": "0" } }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Any-method dead-letters (24h)",
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 6, "y": 1 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=\"outbox.dead_letter\" [24h])) OR vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "orange", "value": 1 }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": { "match": "null+nan", "result": { "text": "0" } }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Unexpected actor errors (24h)",
      "description": "event.name = actor.unexpected_error — an actor method threw something other than a typed ActorError. services/actors/src/lib/actor-error-envelope.ts.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 1 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=\"actor.unexpected_error\" [24h])) OR vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "orange", "value": 1 }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": { "match": "null+nan", "result": { "text": "0" } }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Outbox reclaimed (24h)",
      "description": "A drain claimed a row but the process died before completing it (services/actors/src/actors/outbox-actor.ts #reclaimStale). Not itself an error — delivery is retried — but a rising count means something is crashing mid-delivery.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 1 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=\"outbox.reclaimed\" [24h])) OR vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 1 }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": { "match": "null+nan", "result": { "text": "0" } }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Dead-letters by target actor / method",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 7 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
          "queryType": "range",
          "expr": "sum by (outbox_target_actor, outbox_method) (count_over_time({service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=\"outbox.dead_letter\" [$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outbox_target_actor}}.{{outbox_method}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "custom": { "drawStyle": "bars", "fillOpacity": 60 } },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["sum"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Unexpected actor errors by route",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 7 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
          "queryType": "range",
          "expr": "sum by (actor_route) (count_over_time({service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=\"actor.unexpected_error\" [$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{actor_route}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "custom": { "drawStyle": "bars", "fillOpacity": 60 } },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["sum"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Recent dead-letter and unexpected-error log lines",
      "description": "{service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=~\"outbox.dead_letter|actor.unexpected_error\" — note the pipe filter, not a stream-selector label match (docs/architecture/target-stack.md §7).",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 15 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
          "queryType": "range",
          "expr": "{service_name=\"actors\"} | event_name=~\"outbox.dead_letter|actor.unexpected_error\""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "wrapLogMessage": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Dapr actor calls (Tempo)",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 23 },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "traces",
      "title": "Recent actor invocations",
      "description": "E3 acceptance: \"a Dapr trace for one actor call is visible in Grafana.\" Populated automatically — infra/dapr/config.yaml sets tracing.samplingRate=1 and points every sidecar's OTLP exporter at otel-lgtm:4318, so this needs no extra instrumentation. Verified against this stack's own real traffic (2026-09-10): CallActor/ItemSearchActor/results, CallActor/EmbeddingActor/embed, CallActor/CellarActor/items all present.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 24 },
      "datasource": { "type": "tempo", "uid": "tempo" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "tempo", "uid": "tempo" },
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{resource.service.name=\"actors\" || resource.service.name=\"api\"}",
          "limit": 20
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Dapr runtime (Prometheus: daprd sidecars, placement, scheduler)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Actor method calls / s, by actor type",
      "description": "What actors-dapr delivered to the actor host (sidecar -> app, PUT actors/<Type>/{id}/method/<name>), including reminder callbacks (method/remind/...). Source: dapr_http_client_completed_count, scraped from actors-dapr:9090 by infra/grafana/otel-lgtm/prometheus.yaml.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 35
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (actor_type) (label_replace(rate(dapr_http_client_completed_count{app_id=\"actors\", path=~\"actors/[^/]+/[^/]+/method/.+\"}[$__rate_interval]), \"actor_type\", \"$1\", \"path\", \"actors/([^/]+)/.*\"))",
          "legendFormat": "{{actor_type}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["mean", "max"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Actor method latency p95, by actor type (sidecar -> app)",
      "description": "Round trip from actors-dapr into the actor host and back: the time the actor method itself took, plus the per-actor turn wait inside the app. Dapr reports it in milliseconds. Source: dapr_http_client_roundtrip_latency_bucket.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 35
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, actor_type) (label_replace(rate(dapr_http_client_roundtrip_latency_bucket{app_id=\"actors\", path=~\"actors/[^/]+/[^/]+/method/.+\"}[$__rate_interval]), \"actor_type\", \"$1\", \"path\", \"actors/([^/]+)/.*\")))",
          "legendFormat": "{{actor_type}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["mean", "max"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Pending actor calls (waiting for the per-actor lock)",
      "description": "dapr_runtime_actor_pending_actor_calls. ActorReentrancy is off (infra/dapr/config.yaml, target-stack §8.5), so an actor that calls back into itself inside its own turn deadlocks; that shows up here as a count that climbs and does not come back down.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (actor_type) (dapr_runtime_actor_pending_actor_calls{app_id=\"actors\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{actor_type}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sidecar HTTP API requests / s, by app and status",
      "description": "Calls each app made to its own sidecar (the Dapr HTTP API on :3501 / :3502): actor invocations, reminders, bindings, metadata. Source: dapr_http_server_request_count.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 43
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (app_id, status) (rate(dapr_http_server_request_count[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{app_id}} {{status}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sidecar HTTP API 5xx ratio, by app",
      "description": "Share of sidecar API responses that were 5xx. The `or ... * 0` arm makes a healthy app read 0 rather than no data.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 43
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum by (app_id) (rate(dapr_http_server_request_count{status=~\"5..\"}[$__rate_interval])) or sum by (app_id) (rate(dapr_http_server_request_count[$__rate_interval])) * 0) / sum by (app_id) (rate(dapr_http_server_request_count[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{app_id}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Dapr scrape targets up",
      "description": "1 per daprd / placement / scheduler endpoint Prometheus can scrape. 0 means that process is down or unreachable from otel-lgtm. (In the per-worktree host-run lane the two sidecars are host processes and read 0 by design.)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 50
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "up{job=~\"dapr-sidecar|dapr-control-plane\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Placement: actor hosts registered",
      "description": "dapr_placement_actor_runtimes_total: runtimes that host actor types. This stack has one actor host (services/actors); 0 means no sidecar is offering actor types to placement, and every actor call will fail to find a host.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 50
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(dapr_placement_actor_runtimes_total)",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scheduler: reminder jobs triggered vs undelivered / s",
      "description": "Reminders live in the Dapr scheduler since 1.15 (docker-compose.yml, `scheduler`). Undelivered means the scheduler fired a job and no connected sidecar took it.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 50
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(dapr_scheduler_jobs_triggered_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "triggered"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(dapr_scheduler_jobs_undelivered_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "undelivered"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "services/api (Loki: {service_name=\"api\"})",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 55
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "GraphQL unexpected errors, by field and error",
      "description": "graphql.unexpected_error: exactly the errors the api masked from the client, one event per (error_name, field) per response. Counts events, not requests — the rule api-sustained-request-failures counts distinct request_id instead.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 56
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "queryType": "range",
          "expr": "sum by (graphql_field, error_name) (count_over_time({service_name=\"api\"} | event_name=\"graphql.unexpected_error\" [$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{graphql_field}} {{error_name}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["sum"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Token rejections, by reason",
      "description": "auth.token_rejected. `expired` is routine (INFO); bad_signature / unknown_kid / claim_invalid / malformed / alg_not_allowed / no_subject / other are WARN; `jwks_unavailable` is ERROR and PAGES (rule api-jwks-unavailable): the api cannot verify anyone.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 56
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "queryType": "range",
          "expr": "sum by (auth_reason) (count_over_time({service_name=\"api\"} | event_name=\"auth.token_rejected\" [$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{auth_reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["sum"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Query limit refusals, by code",
      "description": "graphql.limit_refused: QUERY_TOO_DEEP / WIDE / COMPLEX / LARGE / EXPENSIVE / MANY_TOKENS, REQUEST_TOO_LARGE. A burst from one client is someone probing the limits, or a client bug.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 64
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "queryType": "range",
          "expr": "sum by (limit_code) (count_over_time({service_name=\"api\"} | event_name=\"graphql.limit_refused\" [$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{limit_code}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": ["sum"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Actor invocation failures, by actor / method / kind",
      "description": "actor.invocation_failed: failure_kind is status (the actor answered non-2xx), timeout or network. Usually paired with a graphql.unexpected_error on the same request_id — do not add the two panels together.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 64
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "queryType": "range",
          "expr": "sum by (actor_type, actor_method, failure_kind) (count_over_time({service_name=\"api\"} | event_name=\"actor.invocation_failed\" [$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{actor_type}}.{{actor_method}} {{failure_kind}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 60
          }
